// Gemma 4 (Google) — Model configuration
// Source: https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-31B-it (2026-03) plus the
// 26B-A4B, E4B and E2B cards. Verified against each repo's card,
// chat_template.jinja, config.json and generation_config.json.
//
// model_type "gemma4", multimodal (text + image; audio on E2B/E4B/12B per the
// card). Native function calling. All sizes share the same thinking knob and the
// same sampling, so one preset covers them — with ONE deliberate exclusion:
//   - gemma-4-12B publishes NO chat_template.jinja and its tokenizer_config.json
//     carries no template at all, so its enable_thinking support cannot be
//     verified from official files. It is excluded from the match list rather
//     than guessed at.
//
// Context differs by size and that is fine for one ladder: config.json gives
// 262,144 for 31B and 26B-A4B, 131,072 for E4B and E2B (card: "128K tokens
// (E2B/E4B) and 256K tokens (12B, 26B A4B/31B)"). The [32768, 16384, 8192] head
// still leaves ~96K input on the smallest window.
//
// Chat template parameters (chat_template_kwargs):
//   - `enable_thinking: true/false` — the template declares
//     `enable_thinking | default(false)`, i.e. thinking is OFF by default, and
//     the card says "To enable reasoning, set enable_thinking=True". Both modes
//     therefore state it explicitly; this preset's default mode turns thinking ON
//     because Copilot is an agentic harness.
//   - `preserve_thinking` exists (`| default(false)`) and gates whether thinking
//     blocks survive on assistant messages that carry tool_calls. Left UNSET:
//     neither the card nor the template recommends a value, so the checkpoint
//     default stands.
//   - `disable thinking` formatting caveat from the card: every size except E2B
//     and E4B still emits an empty thought block when thinking is off. Harmless,
//     but it explains why none responses differ slightly between sizes.
//
// Sampling: card lists temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=64 and every size's
// generation_config.json ships exactly that. Same values in both modes.
//
// To apply manually, merge "config" into an existing model entry.
// Keep that entry's id, server and actual server model ID unchanged.


{
  "presetVersion": 1,
  "match": ["gemma-4-31B", "gemma-4-26B-A4B", "gemma-4-E4B", "gemma-4-E2B"],
  "meta": {
    "source": "https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-31B-it",
    "verified": "2026-11-10",
    "notes": "Gemma 4 (gemma4, vision, 131K-262K by size). Thinking is OFF by default in the template; both modes state enable_thinking explicitly. preserve_thinking left at the checkpoint default. temp=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=64. gemma-4-12B excluded - it publishes no chat template."
  },
  "config": {
    "displayName": "Gemma 4",
    "family": "gemma4",
    "maxOutputTokens": [32768, 16384, 8192],
    "capabilities": {
      "toolCalling": true,
      "imageInput": true
    },
    "defaultParams": {
      "temperature": 1.0,
      "top_p": 0.95,
      "top_k": 64
    },
    "modelModes": {
      "high": {
        "chat_template_kwargs": {
          "enable_thinking": true
        }
      },
      "none": {
        "chat_template_kwargs": {
          "enable_thinking": false
        }
      }
    },
    "defaultMode": "high"
  }
}
